# The same board, handed a left chart its caller has drawn on already. `left.line(..)` makes the chart's figure, named
# where it is made, `Chart · left`. `Board(left, ..)` sets the board's part to the whole chart (`self.left = left`), a
# lens's put: the part is that chart, so what the chart holds the part holds (#179), and the board's line on its left part
# draws on the figure the chart made. The right part's line makes a figure of its own: two figures, as on the clean side.
# What differs is who draws on the left chart first, and so which value the figure is named by: the caller's chart, or
# the board's part.

route notebooks.side_by_side
step side_by_side/side_by_side
step side_by_side/side_by_side/Chart()
step side_by_side/side_by_side/Chart.line
choice side_by_side/side_by_side/Chart.line/?1
step side_by_side/side_by_side/Chart.line/?1/Chart.create_figure
step side_by_side/side_by_side/Chart()#2
step side_by_side/side_by_side/Board()
step side_by_side/side_by_side/Board.draw
step side_by_side/side_by_side/Board.draw/Chart.line
choice side_by_side/side_by_side/Board.draw/Chart.line/?1
step side_by_side/side_by_side/Board.draw/Chart.line/?1/Chart.create_figure
step side_by_side/side_by_side/Board.draw/Chart.line#2
choice side_by_side/side_by_side/Board.draw/Chart.line#2/?1
step side_by_side/side_by_side/Board.draw/Chart.line#2/?1/Chart.create_figure

